    "Tom Goldstein"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2502.05171",
  "abstract": "This paper introduces a novel language model architecture that can scale up test-time computation by implicitly reasoning in latent space. The model works by iterating a recurrent block, allowing it to perform arbitrarily many computations before emitting a token. This approach stands in contrast to mainstream reasoning models that scale up compute by producing more tokens.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The model uses a **recurrent depth approach**, where a block of layers is iterated multiple times to perform complex computations. This allows the model to **reason in latent space**, without requiring specialized training data or long context windows. The key insight is that **recurrent mechanisms can provide a simple solution for test-time compute scaling**.",
